<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Old Cathedral, Brescia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Duomo Vecchio, Rotonda of Brescia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Old Cathedral of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brescia</a>, known as the Rotonda, is a Romanesque church of circular plan built in the late 11th century on the site of an earlier basilica. It served as the city's winter cathedral, and its crypt preserves older remains. It stands beside the New Cathedral, begun in 1604.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/old-cathedral-brescia.jpg" alt="Old Cathedral, Brescia" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This Photo was taken by Wolfgang Moroder. Feel free to use my photos, but please mention me as the author and send me a message. … · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duomo_vecchio_facciata_Brescia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
